# fydroid-rt: bring up arc0 for adb-over-network while wireless debugging is on.
#
# patchpanel (CrOS host) creates the veth pair vetharc0 <-> arc0 (arc0 =
# 100.115.92.2/30, host end arcbr0 = 100.115.92.1) but deliberately leaves the
# guest end DOWN -- see ArcService::StartArcDeviceDatapath(), which passes
# up=false with the comment "ARC is responsible to set the interface to be up
# to avoid race with netd (b/144545910)". Nothing in fydroid did that, so arc0
# stayed down forever.
#
# adb over network needs it: arc-adbd is disabled on FydeOS (no USB gadget), so
# patchpaneld's adb-proxy -- what actually listens on :5555 on the CrOS side --
# falls back to TCP and connects to 100.115.92.2:5555 (adb_proxy.cc kTcpAddr).
# With arc0 down that connect() never lands and `adb connect <board>:5555`
# fails. Both addresses are compile-time constants on the host side
# (adb_proxy.cc kTcpAddr, datapath.cc kArcAddr, and AddressManager reserves
# exactly one /30 -- 100.115.92.0/30 -- for GuestType::kArc0), so hardcoding
# them here matches the host and cannot drift.
#
# The ip rule is needed because arc0 belongs to no netd network: netd's rules
# steer everything into the selected network's table, where 100.115.92.0/30
# does not resolve. Priority 15000 sits above netd's EXPLICIT_NETWORK (16000)
# so traffic to the host end always uses the main table, which holds arc0's
# connected route.
#
# Gate: persist.adb.tls_server.enable, i.e. Settings > Developer options >
# Wireless debugging (AdbDebuggingManager sets the property to 1 once it has
# the current AP info, and back to 0 when the toggle goes off). The property is
# persistent, and init re-evaluates property triggers against current values on
# boot (QueueAllPropertyActions), so this also re-arms after an ARC restart.

on property:persist.adb.tls_server.enable=1
    trigger fydroid-arc0-net-up

# The seclabel is mandatory: /system/bin/ip is labeled system_file, which is not
# an exec_type, so init cannot compute a domain transition for it and refuses to
# run it ("has incorrect label or no domain transition from u:r:init:s0") even
# in permissive mode. u:r:su:s0 is the same label the container's adbd already
# uses for its root helper (init.usb.rc: adbd --root_seclabel=u:r:su:s0).
on fydroid-arc0-net-up
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/ip link set arc0 up
    # del before add so a re-trigger (toggle off/on) does not stack duplicate
    # rules; the del is expected to fail the first time.
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/ip rule del to 100.115.92.0/30 lookup main pref 15000
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/ip rule add to 100.115.92.0/30 lookup main pref 15000

on property:persist.adb.tls_server.enable=0
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/ip rule del to 100.115.92.0/30 lookup main pref 15000
    exec u:r:su:s0 root root -- /system/bin/ip link set arc0 down
